  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Render the Bike Rental Queue\r\n\r\n### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Look at the `rentals` array in `script.js`.\r\n\r\n2. Complete the `renderRentals()` function.\r\n   * Use `.map()` to go through the `orders` array.\r\n   * Call `createRentalCard()` to create a card for each rental.\r\n   * Display all the cards inside `rentalList`.\r\n\r\n### Check Your Code:\r\n\r\n- Does each rental object create one card?\r\n- Does the rental count match the number of rentals?\r\n- Where does `.map()` repeat the same rendering rule?",
    "submittable": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
    "disable_edit_run_for_submission": "false",
    "widget_view": "false",
    "initial_view_mode": "split",
